MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The control plane now deploys inference services when
FORGEMESH_RUNTIME_LAUNCHER is set, so the documents that still
described the unwired state are brought up to date:

- README: the launcher variables in the configuration table, the
  controller paragraph, a new "部署推理服务" section (the fake loop
  on one machine, restarts, running vLLM) and the fake-runtime compose
  override.
- CHANGELOG: entries for the fake and vLLM process launchers, their
  configuration, the app wiring, Degraded after a restart, the compose
  override and the closed-loop E2E test; the scheduler, deployment and
  compose smoke entries no longer say the app lacks a launcher.
- backup-restore: with a launcher the control plane has a second
  database, the workflow store. Backups take the registry first and the
  workflow store second, and a restore must use files from the same
  set; the scripts, the Python helper and the container commands handle
  both files, and a new section explains what restored services do.
- module-mapping, architecture (known limitations), the Kubernetes
  manifest header and the DELETE 202 description in OpenAPI.
